## FAQ

**How often is the comparison updated?** Once a day, at 07:43 UTC. The badges above show the last run and how many runs there have been.

**Which stores are compared?** {{ retailers | length }} US online stores: {% for r in retailers %}{{ r.name }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. How they were chosen, and why other stores were left out, is in [`docs/sources.md`]({{ blob }}/docs/sources.md).

**Why are so few products compared?** The {{ retailers | length }} stores sell clean, Korean and luxury beauty, and most of their brands are sold by one of them only. In the recon before launch, the share of a store's products also sold by another of the stores was 15% at best and 1 to 7% for most, below the 30% this project aimed for ([decisions D-002, D-018]({{ blob }}/docs/decisions.md)). The compared set grows as more barcodes are read each day.

**How do you know two stores sell the same product?** By barcode first. Name and part-number matches are used only above a threshold whose precision was measured against barcodes, and 100 compared pairs are checked by hand ([method]({{ blob }}/docs/precision.md)).

**What does "price gap" mean?** The highest in-stock price minus the lowest, as a percentage of the lowest, for one product on one day. It is a number, not a judgment of any store.

**Is reading store prices allowed?** Only public product pages and public catalog feeds are read, within each store's robots.txt rules, slowly, and with a name that links back here. No logins, no personal data, no images or descriptions are kept. A store can opt out by email.

**Can I get my own products and competitors?** Yes, see [Want this for your own stores?](#want-this-for-your-own-stores). The first sample is free.

