<details>
<summary><b>For engineers</b></summary>

- **Stack:** Python 3.12, httpx, Protego (robots.txt), Pydantic, DuckDB (SCD2 history), PyArrow (Parquet), GitHub Actions, GitHub Pages. ruff, mypy strict, pytest.
- **Pipeline:** `src/crossprice/run.py`: collect (catalogs, then GTIN probes within a fixed budget) → validate (Pydantic, batch guard) → match (`match.py`) → blind precision (`precision.py`) → compare (`compare.py`) → SCD2 merge (`history.py`) → outputs.
- **Politeness:** one runner per run, at least 3 s between requests per host, one run-wide pace, a 429 pauses the whole run, a challenge stops the store ([decisions D-004, D-016]({{ blob }}/docs/decisions.md)).
- **Docs:** [architecture]({{ blob }}/docs/architecture.md), [decisions]({{ blob }}/docs/decisions.md), [plan]({{ blob }}/docs/plan.md), [sources]({{ blob }}/docs/sources.md), [precision]({{ blob }}/docs/precision.md), [incidents]({{ blob }}/docs/incidents.md), [maintainers]({{ blob }}/docs/maintainers.md).
- **Run locally:** `uv sync && uv run pytest`. Live requests run only on GitHub Actions (`checks.yml` for recon, `daily.yml` for the pipeline).
- **Reuse:** the polite HTTP client, witnesses, validation, history and status come from the store monitor [ecommerce-price-monitor](https://github.com/siddharthkumarx/ecommerce-price-monitor).

</details>

## Data use and compliance

Public prices and stock only, read from public pages within robots.txt rules. No personal data, no images, no product descriptions. Prices are shown as found; differences are shown as numbers. Store and product names belong to their owners. A store that wants to be left out can email [{{ pub.email }}](mailto:{{ pub.email }}); it is removed within 24 hours.

